Description: Disable sanitize_c_array_bounds config to fix clang-19 ICE
 clang-19 crashes (SIGSEGV, exit code 139) when -fsanitize=array-bounds is
 combined with std::strong_ordering / spaceship operator (operator<=>). The
 crash occurs in services/network/public/cpp/permissions_policy/
 origin_with_possible_wildcards.cc and potentially other files. The entire
 sanitize_c_array_bounds config is a Google-internal runtime hardening option
 not required for Debian packaging, so disabling it is safe.
 Applies after Debian Chromium llvm-22/ignore-for-ubsan.patch which already
 removed the -fsanitize-ignore-for-ubsan-feature and -Wno-unsafe-buffer lines.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-04-10

diff --git a/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn b/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
index d5afc03..0f8b874 100644
--- a/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
@@ -1875,18 +1875,10 @@ config("clang_warning_suppression") {
 #
 # See also: https://crbug.com/40891132#comment10
 config("sanitize_c_array_bounds") {
-  if (!is_ubsan && is_clang && !(is_asan && target_cpu == "x86")) {
-    cflags = [
-      "-fsanitize=array-bounds",
-      "-fsanitize-trap=array-bounds",
-
-      # Some code users feature detection to determine if UBSAN (or any
-      # sanitizer) is enabled, they then do expensive debug like operations. We
-      # want to suppress this behaviour since we want to keep performance costs
-      # as low as possible while having these checks.
-
-    ]
-  }
+  # Disabled for Debian builds: clang-19 crashes (ICE/SIGSEGV) when
+  # -fsanitize=array-bounds is combined with std::strong_ordering / spaceship
+  # operator. This is a Google-internal performance config not needed for
+  # Debian packaging.
 }

 config("rustc_revision") {
